    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  The principles of <span class=\"learn-keyword\">genetics and evolution</span> are not just theoretical — they have practical, real-world applications in agriculture, medicine, and conservation that directly affect food production, healthcare, and biodiversity.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Applications in Agriculture</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Application</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Selective breeding</td><td>Choosing parent organisms with desirable traits (high yield, disease resistance) to breed the next generation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Hybridization</td><td>Crossing two different varieties or species to combine desirable traits in the offspring</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Genetic engineering</td><td>Directly altering an organism's DNA to introduce or remove specific traits</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>GMOs</td><td>Genetically Modified Organisms — organisms whose genetic material has been altered using genetic engineering techniques, e.g., pest-resistant crops</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Applications in Medicine</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Blood transfusion:</strong> Understanding blood group genetics (A, B, AB, O) ensures compatible, safe transfusions between donor and recipient</li>\n  <li><strong>Sickle cell study:</strong> Genetics research has revealed how the sickle cell allele is inherited and how it relates to malaria resistance, informing screening and counselling programmes</li>\n  <li><strong>Genetic counselling:</strong> Advising couples on the risk of passing on inherited disorders to their children, based on genetic analysis</li>\n  <li><strong>Cloning:</strong> Producing genetically identical copies of cells or organisms, with potential medical applications in tissue repair and research</li>\n  <li><strong>IVF (In Vitro Fertilization):</strong> A medical technique where fertilization occurs outside the body, helping couples facing fertility challenges to conceive</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Role of Evolution in Biodiversity and Conservation</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Understanding evolutionary relationships helps conservationists prioritise which species and genetic diversity to protect, predict how species may respond to environmental change (such as climate change), and manage breeding programmes for endangered species to maintain healthy genetic diversity.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Distinguish \"selective breeding\" (choosing existing organisms with desired traits to breed) from \"genetic engineering\" (directly modifying DNA) — WAEC frequently tests this distinction.\n</div>\n",
