    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Advances in genetics — cloning, stem cell research, and GMOs — raise important <span class=\"learn-keyword\">ethical, social, and economic questions</span> that societies, including Nigeria, must grapple with alongside the scientific possibilities.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Ethical Debates on Cloning</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Cloning raises questions about the moral status of cloned organisms, potential misuse (such as human reproductive cloning), and whether creating genetically identical copies of living things is ethically acceptable, particularly for humans.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Ethical Debates on Stem Cell Research</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Stem cells</span> are unspecialised cells capable of developing into different cell types, offering potential treatments for many diseases. However, when derived from human embryos, this research raises ethical concerns about the moral status of the embryo.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Advantages and Disadvantages of GMOs</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Advantages</th><th>Disadvantages</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Higher crop yields and pest resistance</td><td>Potential unknown long-term health effects</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Improved nutritional content in some crops</td><td>Risk of reduced biodiversity if GMO crops dominate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reduced need for chemical pesticides</td><td>Economic dependency on seed-producing companies</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Importance of Conserving Genetic Resources</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Preserving a wide range of genetic diversity — in crops, livestock, and wild species — is important because it provides a reservoir of traits (such as disease resistance or drought tolerance) that may be needed for future breeding programmes or to cope with environmental change.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Relevance to Nigeria's Development</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">For Nigeria, responsible application of genetics — improved crop varieties suited to local conditions, genetic screening for inherited conditions like sickle cell disease, and conservation of indigenous plant and animal genetic resources — can support food security, public health, and sustainable development, provided ethical and regulatory safeguards are in place.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> When discussing GMOs or cloning in an essay or short answer, present a balanced view — mention both benefits and potential risks/concerns, rather than a one-sided argument.\n</div>\n",
